1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:03,504
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:30,549 --> 00:01:31,717
[TETIA] Wow!

3
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:33,928
You're so fast, Coco!

4
00:01:34,887 --> 00:01:37,598
[laughter]

5
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,850
Very fast, indeed!

6
00:01:39,892 --> 00:01:41,894
Agott was speeding along
as well.

7
00:01:41,936 --> 00:01:43,062
Now I know why!

8
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:44,855
It was thanks to the shoes
you prepared for her!

9
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:46,481
[screeches]

10
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,400
What was that?
What's going on?

11
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:50,069
What did I do to Agott?

12
00:01:50,109 --> 00:01:51,278
It's fine, really.

13
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:53,655
She is wearing them, isn't she?

14
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:55,991
I would take that to mean
she likes your spell.

15
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:57,409
[Coco gasps]

16
00:01:57,910 --> 00:02:00,370
Straight lines
are your specialty, yes?

17
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:02,748
Perhaps there are other places
they'll come in handy.

18
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:05,375
Uh, Master Qifrey?
She's not listening.

19
00:02:05,417 --> 00:02:06,418
[QIFREY] Uh?

20
00:02:06,585 --> 00:02:08,211
[COCO] I had a smart thought
like Agott!

21
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:10,338
[TETIA] Uh... Master Qifrey?

22
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:16,678
Is anything the matter?

23
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:20,474
Possibly. This is Alaira's hat.

24
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:21,558
[both gasp]

25
00:02:21,767 --> 00:02:24,061
[QIFREY] Hats are very important
to witches.

26
00:02:24,103 --> 00:02:26,105
- We don't let them go unless...
- [all gasp]

27
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:32,861
[QIFREY] A golem?

28
00:02:32,945 --> 00:02:35,781
A forbidden spell this ancient
shouldn't still be active!

29
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:39,785
It's them.
The Brimmed Caps did this!

30
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:43,497
- [Qifrey grunts]
- [BOTH] Master Qifrey!

31
00:02:43,914 --> 00:02:46,041
[girls screaming]

32
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:51,130
FORBIDDEN MAGIC

33
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:53,548
[panting]

34
00:02:55,926 --> 00:02:58,553
[EUINI]
So, we're running away, but...

35
00:02:58,595 --> 00:02:59,972
Where to?

36
00:03:00,014 --> 00:03:01,264
[panting]

37
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:03,767
That was a Brimmed Cap!

38
00:03:04,143 --> 00:03:07,146
No, we can't do this!
We, uh...

39
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:10,899
[Euini whimpers]

40
00:03:12,567 --> 00:03:13,777
[Euini grunts]

41
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:23,662
[SASARAN] Well,
isn't this interesting?

42
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:26,957
You actually managed
to hide from me.

43
00:03:26,999 --> 00:03:28,750
[laughs]

44
00:03:28,792 --> 00:03:32,838
Lucky for me,
I adore hide-and-seek.

45
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,174
Ready or not, here I come!

46
00:03:35,214 --> 00:03:36,257
[myrphons squeak]

47
00:03:36,884 --> 00:03:38,177
[EUINI] Huh?

48
00:03:38,217 --> 00:03:39,678
[Richeh gasps]

49
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:46,225
[Euini gasps softly]

50
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:47,728
That's right.

51
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,897
My cloak no longer...

52
00:03:50,271 --> 00:03:51,940
- [myrphons screaming]
- [RICHEH] Quiet!

53
00:03:51,982 --> 00:03:55,276
[myrphons continue screaming]

54
00:03:58,363 --> 00:04:01,449
[SASARAN] Who hides
away in darkness?

55
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:04,995
The sinner, enshrouding their
nasty little secrets.

56
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:09,624
The weakling scurrying in fear
for their safety.

57
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:13,420
And the hunter,
lying in wait for their prey.

58
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:17,674
Question is...
Which one are you?

59
00:04:19,258 --> 00:04:20,510
- [RICHEH] It's gone!
- [AGOTT] It vanished!

60
00:04:20,594 --> 00:04:23,931
[SASARAN] You can rule out
the latter category

61
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:27,976
because the only hunter here
is me.

62
00:04:28,018 --> 00:04:29,728
[wind howling]

63
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:31,605
- [Euini gasps]
- [BOTH] Euini!

64
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:33,732
[Euini whimpers]

65
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:35,358
Please, help me!

66
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,945
- Close your eyes, now!
- Richeh!

67
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:40,239
- [EUINI] Ah!
- [AGOTT] Euini!

68
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:43,242
You can stand, can't you?

69
00:04:43,282 --> 00:04:44,993
Come on Richeh, let's go!

70
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:47,746
Have fun blathering
at a dust cloud!

71
00:04:49,164 --> 00:04:50,916
[panting]

72
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,419
[AGOTT] The magic affecting
the cave makes it impossible

73
00:04:54,461 --> 00:04:56,088
for us to fly away.

74
00:04:56,130 --> 00:04:59,591
And stretching out the stones
will only take us so far.

75
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:02,970
This isn't a foe we can escape
through cleverness or trickery.

76
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:05,304
If even Alaira
was no match for them,

77
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:08,349
what can I possibly be
expected to do? [gasps]

78
00:05:15,816 --> 00:05:18,026
[gasps] Of course!

79
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:19,820
[EUINI] What is it?

80
00:05:20,319 --> 00:05:21,989
[AGOTT] When Alaira crossed
the gap in the road,

81
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:24,616
she froze the air under her feet
and skated forward.

82
00:05:27,119 --> 00:05:28,369
- What if we freeze...
- [RICHEH] There.

83
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,496
...the road itself?

84
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,832
Then the gaps in the seals
won't be a problem!

85
00:05:31,873 --> 00:05:33,332
[pen scratching]

86
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:35,294
[AGOTT]
That should about do it.

87
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:48,182
We can slide
faster than we can run!

88
00:05:53,312 --> 00:05:55,814
Well done, Richeh,
now let's be off!

89
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:59,276
- Come on! Hurry up! Go!
- [EUINI] Uh?

90
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:04,072
♪

91
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:12,539
[Euini yelping]

92
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:14,666
[EUINI] Agott,
why do your Sylph Shoes

93
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:16,084
have such incredible speed?

94
00:06:16,126 --> 00:06:17,794
[AGOTT]
I'd rather not discuss it!

95
00:06:17,836 --> 00:06:20,047
We need to freeze
the path ahead, and quickly!

96
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:22,423
[EUINI] Right! Allow me!

97
00:06:32,684 --> 00:06:33,894
[Euini gasps softly]

98
00:06:33,935 --> 00:06:36,063
At this rate,
he's going to catch up.

99
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:38,190
Use a wind spell,
we'll move faster!

100
00:06:38,232 --> 00:06:39,398
[RICHEH] I...

101
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:42,069
I can't.

102
00:06:42,361 --> 00:06:45,780
I don't know that many
different spells.

103
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,199
Just my own.

104
00:06:47,241 --> 00:06:49,076
[EUINI] Oh, well...

105
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:51,161
[RICHEH] Huh?

106
00:06:51,203 --> 00:06:53,872
Here. You can use my spells.

107
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:57,125
It's embarrassing,
but I'm glad I wrote them out.

108
00:06:59,586 --> 00:07:02,005
If they can be of help to you.

109
00:07:02,047 --> 00:07:03,590
♪

110
00:07:21,316 --> 00:07:23,818
[AGOTT] This was my big chance
to take the test.

111
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:26,280
So why did I have
to get dragged into this?

112
00:07:26,321 --> 00:07:28,823
[TETIA] Why did I have
to get dragged into...

113
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:32,327
[AGOTT] The day
that dragon was after us,

114
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,746
Tetia asked the same question.

115
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,165
Calamities of this magnitude

116
00:07:37,207 --> 00:07:39,709
don't befall
ordinary apprentices.

117
00:07:40,294 --> 00:07:43,588
It's clear the Brimmed Caps
are after something special.

118
00:07:44,631 --> 00:07:46,507
And it isn't us.

119
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:52,847
[EUINI] Agott?

120
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:55,892
[AGOTT] You won't find
who you're looking for!

121
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:57,144
She's not here!

122
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,395
She's gone.

123
00:07:58,437 --> 00:08:00,521
Taken away from us
by the Knights Moralis.

124
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:04,067
They erased her memories,
and returned her to her village!

125
00:08:04,443 --> 00:08:07,737
Therefore, to pursue us further
is pointless!

126
00:08:07,779 --> 00:08:10,782
Because the Outsider
whom you seek

127
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:13,243
no longer resides
within our atelier!

128
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:15,996
[Agott grunts]

129
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:20,125
[SASARAN] A declaration
worthy of an apprentice

130
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:24,503
to those foremost of liars,
the Pointed Caps.

131
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:28,549
You've learned well
the art of deception.

132
00:08:29,550 --> 00:08:32,179
- [RICHEH] Agott!
- [Richeh and Euini panting]

133
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:35,015
- Agott?
- [EUINI] Agott!

134
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:39,019
[SASARAN] Poor dear.

135
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:43,773
The Pointed Caps
of the past were nasty sinners.

136
00:08:43,815 --> 00:08:46,776
The Pointed Caps
of the present are weaklings

137
00:08:46,818 --> 00:08:49,029
who fear their own power.

138
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:51,614
Their weakness stifles you.

139
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:54,868
Binds you to the tyranny
of their rules,

140
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:59,414
your vast potential unrealized.

141
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:03,668
[AGOTT]
Smells like Conjuring Ink.

142
00:09:04,336 --> 00:09:06,671
[SASARAN] The salvation
you must dream of

143
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:08,923
may be found in forbidden magic.

144
00:09:09,548 --> 00:09:13,220
You could grow up this instant,
if you wished it so.

145
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:16,431
Or you could remain
forever a child.

146
00:09:17,015 --> 00:09:19,684
You could become
your ideal self,

147
00:09:19,726 --> 00:09:23,855
with no need to hide your magic
from the eyes of others.

148
00:09:23,897 --> 00:09:25,815
Even without your shoes...

149
00:09:25,857 --> 00:09:28,567
- [Agott whimpers]
- [SASARAN]...you could soar.

150
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:31,071
You could go
wherever you wanted!

151
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:32,571
As you might have noticed,

152
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:35,867
I've liberated myself
from the shackles of flesh!

153
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:39,578
There will come a day
when the world remembers

154
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:43,708
what kind of hat
witches were meant to wear.

155
00:09:44,876 --> 00:09:48,338
That day is inevitable,
I assure you.

156
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,799
We simply seek
to hasten its arrival.

157
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:53,552
And to that end,

158
00:09:53,592 --> 00:09:55,929
- there must be sacrifice.
- [Agott grunts]

159
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,347
Agott!

160
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:00,058
[SASARAN] If she learns

161
00:10:00,225 --> 00:10:03,520
the friend who lied to save her
has fallen to harm,

162
00:10:03,562 --> 00:10:07,857
and the means to undo
the damage lie within reach,

163
00:10:07,899 --> 00:10:10,193
with so much to be lost,

164
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:14,072
could she turn down
the miracle our magic offers?

165
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:17,909
Children are loath
to face life's tests,

166
00:10:17,951 --> 00:10:20,120
but such is how
they learn and grow.

167
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:25,750
In this case, I've devised
a little test for her.

168
00:10:25,792 --> 00:10:29,254
And you, child,
will learn an excellent...

169
00:10:29,754 --> 00:10:32,006
painful lesson.

170
00:10:35,218 --> 00:10:36,595
[Agott yells]

171
00:10:37,095 --> 00:10:38,430
[EASTHIES] In some cases,

172
00:10:38,472 --> 00:10:40,432
the Brimmed Caps
tattoo their bodies

173
00:10:40,474 --> 00:10:42,183
with grotesque seals.

174
00:10:42,559 --> 00:10:43,684
[Agott gasps]

175
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:45,103
Are you...

176
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:47,105
No! You mustn't!

177
00:10:47,147 --> 00:10:50,484
I can't let everything I have
be taken away from me!

178
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:54,904
I still need to prove
myself to... [breathes shakily]

179
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:57,157
[RICHEH] Agott!

180
00:10:57,949 --> 00:11:00,577
When you fall, grab this!

181
00:11:00,619 --> 00:11:03,037
When I fall?

182
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:08,460
[Agott grunts]

183
00:11:10,128 --> 00:11:11,463
[Richeh grunts]

184
00:11:13,006 --> 00:11:14,299
[Agott gasps]

185
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:19,638
[thudding]

186
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:22,098
What just happened to the ice?

187
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,683
[RICHEH] Euini broke it
from under that witch's feet.

188
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:26,603
If you leave the path,

189
00:11:26,645 --> 00:11:28,687
you get caught
in the labyrinth, right?

190
00:11:29,481 --> 00:11:31,024
So in theory,

191
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:33,985
the same thing should happen
if the path leaves you.

192
00:11:34,277 --> 00:11:35,862
Good idea.

193
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:38,448
But hasn't that Brimmed Cap

194
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:41,159
been flying around here
all along?

195
00:11:42,494 --> 00:11:45,163
[EUINI] Looks like
Agott's safe and sound.

196
00:11:45,205 --> 00:11:47,081
What a relief that it worked!

197
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:53,880
To think covering up
for my own weaknesses

198
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:56,216
could lead to something useful.

199
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:57,800
I'm so happy.

200
00:11:57,842 --> 00:12:00,345
Maybe I'm not so hopeless
after all!

201
00:12:01,388 --> 00:12:03,848
Stop and listen to me, Master!

202
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:04,891
I...

203
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:07,810
I'm not as hopeless
as I thought I was!

204
00:12:08,395 --> 00:12:12,273
I'm not as hopeless
as you've always told me I was!

205
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:16,819
Perhaps being unable
to do the things

206
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:18,238
that others can

207
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,699
is actually an opportunity

208
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:23,535
to discover the things
I can do that others can't!

209
00:12:23,577 --> 00:12:25,245
[SASARAN] Very well said!

210
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:27,205
[Euini yells, grunts]

211
00:12:27,247 --> 00:12:29,207
[SASARAN] And perhaps
if you'd made

212
00:12:29,249 --> 00:12:32,293
better use of your abilities
and remained hidden,

213
00:12:32,335 --> 00:12:35,171
I would have been willing
to leave you be.

214
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:36,423
[EUINI] Help me...

215
00:12:36,715 --> 00:12:39,467
[SASARAN] Being cloaked
in shadow suggests a dark side.

216
00:12:39,509 --> 00:12:42,262
A quality
you're sorely lacking.

217
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:44,431
Oh, here's an idea:

218
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:48,226
I'll grant you a new form
you'll be desperate to hide.

219
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:52,647
[RICHEH] Flying all along?

220
00:12:52,689 --> 00:12:55,275
That shouldn't be possible.

221
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:56,693
Supposedly,

222
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:59,404
if something's not making
direct contact with the road,

223
00:12:59,446 --> 00:13:01,948
then it should be
affected by the ancient spell

224
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,450
of the Romonons.

225
00:13:03,491 --> 00:13:05,868
But if that doesn't apply
to the Brimmed Caps,

226
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:07,746
we're still in danger!

227
00:13:07,786 --> 00:13:09,372
Let's find Euini.

228
00:13:09,414 --> 00:13:11,832
We need to get back
to Master Qifrey fast.

229
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,419
- [AGOTT] Euini!
- [RICHEH] Euini!

230
00:13:14,461 --> 00:13:15,836
[AGOTT] Euini!

231
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:23,010
- [Agott gasps]
- Euini?

232
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:24,887
[rustling]

233
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,265
[Euini muttering indistinctly]

234
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:30,226
[Euini groaning]

235
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,361
[rustling]

236
00:13:41,571 --> 00:13:43,281
[Richeh gasps softly]

237
00:13:45,116 --> 00:13:47,702
[Euini groaning]

238
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:55,585
[Richeh gasps]

239
00:13:55,627 --> 00:13:57,671
[Euini grunting]

240
00:14:07,514 --> 00:14:09,223
Agott...

241
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:14,312
Richeh, please, help me.
[grunting]

242
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:16,272
[Euini growling]

243
00:14:24,531 --> 00:14:25,906
[both gasp]

244
00:14:28,909 --> 00:14:32,413
[Euini huffing]

245
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,882
[Euini growling]

246
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:49,972
[Richeh gasps]

247
00:14:50,889 --> 00:14:53,601
No... Euini!

248
00:14:58,857 --> 00:15:00,567
[gasps] Richeh!

249
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:03,778
We have to do something!
We have to help Euini!

250
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:05,946
[SASARAN] Hmm.

251
00:15:07,866 --> 00:15:10,159
[SASARAN]
Isn't that fascinating?

252
00:15:10,201 --> 00:15:13,329
To think the scalewolf fur
from his cloak

253
00:15:13,371 --> 00:15:15,206
would integrate with the spell.

254
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:16,332
You monster.

255
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:18,334
[SASARAN] You must understand,

256
00:15:18,376 --> 00:15:22,171
information on forbidden spells
has grown scarce over time.

257
00:15:22,213 --> 00:15:23,423
[chuckles]
We oft don't know

258
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:25,842
what they'll do
until we cast them.

259
00:15:25,884 --> 00:15:28,219
Not the result I was expecting,

260
00:15:28,261 --> 00:15:31,138
but I suppose it worked out
proper good that, eh?

261
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,559
I've heard enough out of you!
Turn Euini back to normal!

262
00:15:34,601 --> 00:15:39,146
[SASARAN] If it is your wish
to save the boy, by all means,

263
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:41,441
I invite you to do so!

264
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:44,943
Magic has the power
to grant all our wishes.

265
00:15:44,985 --> 00:15:48,072
What happens next is up to you.

266
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:04,088
Where are you going, Richeh?

267
00:16:05,548 --> 00:16:07,133
Isn't it obvious?

268
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:08,593
I'm saving Euini.

269
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:11,137
Because...

270
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:14,474
as much as I hate doing things
I don't want to,

271
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:17,143
I hate abandoning friends
even more!

272
00:16:18,603 --> 00:16:20,146
You agree, don't you?

273
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:22,064
Yes, of course I do.

274
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,733
But what about the myrphons?

275
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:27,320
They're scared,
and we're responsible for them.

276
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:29,113
I know it's no time for tests,

277
00:16:29,155 --> 00:16:31,699
but we should at least
get them back to their flock.

278
00:16:31,741 --> 00:16:34,744
And someone has to report back
about what's happened here.

279
00:16:35,662 --> 00:16:38,748
To Alaira, and to Euini.

280
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:41,208
Why don't we split up?

281
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,336
I'll go after Euini.

282
00:16:43,670 --> 00:16:45,797
You get the myrphons
safely to the exit.

283
00:16:45,839 --> 00:16:47,381
[RICHEH]
I want to go after Euini!

284
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,383
Why are you the one
who gets to decide?

285
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:51,845
[AGOTT] I know more spells
than you do, Richeh.

286
00:16:51,886 --> 00:16:53,220
I'm more prepared.

287
00:16:53,888 --> 00:16:55,807
The spells at your disposal
are limited

288
00:16:55,849 --> 00:16:58,392
to those you have
an interest in.

289
00:16:58,434 --> 00:17:01,771
You can't be flexible
in unexpected circumstances.

290
00:17:01,813 --> 00:17:05,650
Sorry if this sounds harsh,
but it's true.

291
00:17:05,692 --> 00:17:08,152
As you are,
you can't help Euini.

292
00:17:22,959 --> 00:17:24,210
[Richeh inhales]

293
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:27,045
[Richeh sighs]

294
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,340
[wind howling]

295
00:17:36,848 --> 00:17:39,475
[brushbuddy squeaking]

296
00:17:54,949 --> 00:17:56,534
[brushbuddy sighs]

297
00:17:57,702 --> 00:18:00,038
[brushbuddy squeaking]

298
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:04,333
[BRUSHBUDDY] Mm?

299
00:18:09,005 --> 00:18:11,507
[brushbuddy squeaking]

300
00:18:20,725 --> 00:18:21,851
Brushbuddy?

301
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:23,310
[Coco gasps softly]

302
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:25,438
♪

303
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:31,652
[COCO] Uh?

304
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:51,464
[COCO]
What happened back there?

305
00:18:51,798 --> 00:18:53,967
The serpent gate attacked us.

306
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:56,636
The ground caved in.

307
00:18:56,928 --> 00:18:58,387
And then,

308
00:18:58,805 --> 00:19:01,849
Master Qifrey protected me.

309
00:19:03,517 --> 00:19:05,185
Master Qifrey?

310
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:07,814
Tetia?

311
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:08,982
[Coco gasps softly]

312
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:11,985
[Coco breathes shakily]

313
00:19:16,322 --> 00:19:19,283
Is he all right?

314
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:22,286
His glasses are broken.

315
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:25,498
And he's bleeding.

316
00:19:28,835 --> 00:19:30,252
[Coco gasps]

317
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:36,843
Uh... sorry about that.

318
00:19:36,884 --> 00:19:39,804
- Your glasses were cracked.
- [Tetia groans softly]

319
00:19:39,846 --> 00:19:43,265
- [COCO] I wanted to make sure--
- Hush. Listen.

320
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:48,228
[distant clattering]

321
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:53,026
[QIFREY] Something's out there.

322
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:14,714
[FEMALE ROMONON]
There are witches...

323
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:18,134
Witches among us.

324
00:20:18,176 --> 00:20:22,304
[MALE ROMONON]
Witches gave us these forms.

325
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:25,766
Vile, contemptible witches.

326
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:29,478
Um, Master, could they be...

327
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:32,106
Yes. Romonon citizens,

328
00:20:32,148 --> 00:20:35,442
living on still
as golden statues.

329
00:20:35,484 --> 00:20:37,028
[Qifrey grunts]

330
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,112
[BOTH] Master!

331
00:20:38,154 --> 00:20:40,073
[Qifrey groans]

332
00:20:40,114 --> 00:20:41,949
[COCO] You're badly hurt.

333
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:46,370
[gasps] We're in trouble here.

334
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:49,373
Their resentment towards
witches is deeply held.

335
00:20:49,415 --> 00:20:51,291
[winces]

336
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:54,545
Therefore, we should assume

337
00:20:54,587 --> 00:20:57,255
they'll attack us,
given the opportunity.

338
00:21:01,259 --> 00:21:03,637
You need to stay
right where you are.

339
00:21:04,013 --> 00:21:06,473
They won't be able
to sense your presence.

340
00:21:06,849 --> 00:21:10,728
As for my cloak,
its spell appears to be ruined.

341
00:21:13,022 --> 00:21:16,150
You got injured
trying to protect us.

342
00:21:16,192 --> 00:21:17,484
[Coco gasps]

343
00:21:20,613 --> 00:21:22,031
[QIFREY] I did.

344
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:24,242
And I will...

345
00:21:24,282 --> 00:21:26,326
because I'm your master.

346
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:35,293
- Hear me.
- [BOTH] Huh?

347
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:37,213
[QIFREY] Both of you.

348
00:21:38,505 --> 00:21:40,340
Stay close to me.

349
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:47,347
Very close.

350
00:21:50,143 --> 00:21:51,393
[wind blows]

351
00:21:51,978 --> 00:21:53,479
♪

352
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:08,119
[♪ closing theme song playing]

